              "source": "commons-desc-page"
            },
            "ImageDescription": {
              "value": "\"Ko-i-staun foot soldier in summer costume. The original sketch made into a lithograph, plate 12 by R. Carrick for publishing in 'Afghaunistan' by Lieutenant <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=James_Rattray&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"James Rattray (page does not exist)\">James Rattray</a>. This Kohistani is Mir Alam, formerly one of a band of noted robbers based in the Ghoorbund Pass (on the high road to Toorkistaun north-west of Begraum). on the road to Turkestan, north-west of Begram. Rattray wrote: \"Coistaun has always been remarkable for the war-like character of its inhabitants, who average some forty thousand families famous for the efficiency and excellence of their Pyadas (foot-soldiery)\"...",
              "source": "commons-desc-page"
            },
